# managed via cape-host-config.deb.  Mode 0440 root:root —
# anything else and sudo refuses to load it ("sudoers is world-
# writable" / "sudoers is owned by uid X, should be 0").
#
# Grants the cape service account passwordless sudo so operators
# SSH'd in as `cape` can run systemctl / virsh / journalctl without
# needing a second account.  Matches install-nestedvirt.sh::
# configure_cape_admin_access which dropped /etc/sudoers.d/90-cape-
# admin with the same line at first boot.
#
# Justification: cape is the CAPE service account and already owns
# /opt/CAPEv2/storage/, /home/cape/, the libvirt connection, and the
# postgres `cape` DB role.  Giving it sudo doesn't widen the blast
# radius materially over what cape can already do, and it eliminates
# the operator-needs-ubuntu-key second-account pattern the bootstrap-
# from-QCOW2 path required.
cape ALL=(ALL) NOPASSWD:ALL
